"""Mostly negative onset offsets and sparse Chinese / shell lexical responses.

At a document's first token the pulse depends on ordinary word and character
classes. Later, Chinese selfhood/autonomy, markets, value, on-site words,
and finality are positive cues; initiality is negative.
Repeated middle dots have a separate negative response. For ${ openings,
shell cues or quoting give a positive response, suppressed by JavaScript cues. Uncovered
positions are left near zero. These are approximations, not token lookup.
