The strongest response is to small letter pieces attached to a word fragment
of at most three letters. Longer words and whole, space-prefixed words get
little response. UTF-8 continuation-byte pieces get a separate boost.
The response is adjusted for script, case, and the size of the new piece;
a small document-initial correction handles the absence of a preceding token.
