Separate characters fire strongly; larger tokens containing them fire less.
Common compounds (air, illness, electricity) weaken the separate-character
response too.  Korean 기 and its nominalizing forms are another strong
spelling family.  Romanized qi can straddle a token boundary.  Short u-continuations
after q receive a negative response.  Other text is assigned zero.
