"""Layer 1, MLP down-projection, component 5151: the letters "am" inside a word.

Plain-terms reading: the component watches for the letters "a" "m" when they sit
inside a word piece, and its sign and size depend on the letter just before the "a":
  - after "s" (Sam, sam, Zusammen, Gesamt, Ses-ame, Russian "сам"): positive, about +5;
  - after "z" (zam, gez-am-e): mildly positive, about +2.5;
  - after "o" (foam, Silo-am, chorio-am): negative, about -5;
  - after "e" (ste-am, gle-am, aming): mildly negative, about -1.7.
Whole English words that contain "am" but are not fragments (team, beam, seam, dream,
cream, stream, sample...) stay near zero, so they are skipped. The word "same" is skipped
after "the", "a", "this", "that" (as in "the same"); elsewhere it reads as a fragment and
is positive, about +3. Only short pieces (up to 4 letters) count, plus German "-ammen"
compounds, so long English words do not fire.
Everything else predicts 0.

The carry is the last two characters of the document's text so far, and the previous
word, so the letter before a token's "a" can be read even when it sits at the end of the
previous token. A new document resets the carry.
