"""Approximate a tu-versus-to spelling contrast.

Short u-initial continuations after t are positive; o-initial ones are
negative. Fragment length and following letters adjust their strength.
There are weaker responses inside short tokens and on the next fragment.
Latin, Cyrillic and Greek share spelling rules, with script/diacritic
amplitude discounts and suppression of identifier-like case changes.
State keeps the final two spelling characters and resets per document.
Unmatched positions are zero, except for a small document-start bias.
