Standalone and prefix-like quotes are strongest, especially escaped double
quotes. Quotes fused with closing punctuation are weaker. Apostrophes attached
to letters or digits are largely suppressed. The previous token's final
character distinguishes whitespace-adjacent quotes from word-adjacent ones.
Backticks, primes and the phonetic stress mark have separate positive levels;
a negative offset handles document starts. Ordinary tokens otherwise get zero.
The levels summarize training examples, not a table of token identities.
